From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:14:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] oleaut32: Say True and False in Chinese and Russian as
 Windows does.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

VarBstrFromBool and VariantChangeType with VARIANT_LOCALBOOL turn a
boolean into the locale's word for it. Windows 11 (build 29671) keeps
"True" and "False" for Chinese, simplified and traditional, and says
"Истина" for True in Russian; Wine said 真 and 假, and Правда. As VBScript
converts booleans this way, CStr(True) and "x" & True read 真 on a
Chinese system, where Windows scripts read True.

The two strings get a context of their own, apart from oleview's, with
every other language's translation kept (English, German, French and
Japanese measured the same as Windows).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit fcc0548ed6298ef071479af75884920841427ae0)

diff --git a/dlls/oleaut32/oleaut32.rc b/dlls/oleaut32/oleaut32.rc
index 9daeebde38c..a4c8693541e 100644
--- a/dlls/oleaut32/oleaut32.rc
+++ b/dlls/oleaut32/oleaut32.rc
@@ -26,8 +26,8 @@ LANGUAGE LANG_ENGLISH, SUBLANG_DEFAULT
 
 STRINGTABLE
 {
-  IDS_TRUE  "True"
-  IDS_FALSE "False"
+  IDS_TRUE  "#msgctxt#variant#True"
+  IDS_FALSE "#msgctxt#variant#False"
   IDS_YES   "Yes"
   IDS_NO    "No"
   IDS_ON    "On"
